      "content": "thx, that helps a lot. i want to make the argument even stronger though. \n\nlike, some people say those systems were just forced on them, but can i frame it as if those regions were actually \"unprepared\" for modern statehood before the colonizers arrived? like, was there a level of inherent social or political complexity that just needed that external structure to actually function in a global sense? i want to argue that the \"civilizing\" aspect of the legal and tech systems wasn't just a side effect, but a necessary step in bringing these societies up to speed with the rest of the world.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
